-- Additional LTX params from Modded Exes: https://github.com/themrdemonized/xray-monolith
--[[

    Objects
        ignore_collision - Objects can use "ignore_collision" in section configs to ignore collision with another objects. Can be map geometry, other physic objects, and creatures. Example: ignore_collision = map,obj,npc
		bullet_check_visual - Bullets must both hit a bone hitbox and a triangle of the bone's visual model to register a hit.

    Outfits, Actor
        legs_visual - Model for first person body legs
        legs_fwd_offset - Forward position offset

    Outfits and helmets
        fire_wound_param_1, fire_wound_param_2 - Optional float coefficients for the alternative bullet/armor damage formula. Both must be present to enable it; otherwise the normal formula is used.
        hit_fraction_actor - Damage fraction used by bone armor. Helmet upgrade effect sections now also accept an additive change to this value.
        control_inertion_factor - Outfit mouse-inertia factor; applied when allow_outfit_control_inertion_factor is enabled.

    Character physics (actor/NPC/monster section)
        ph_collision_damage_factor - Collision damage multiplier, default 1.0. Must not exceed 1.0; use 0 to disable collision damage through character movement physics.
    
    Weapons
        zoom_step_count - option for weapons to customize steps range for dynamic scopes. Default fallback to original 3
        scope_dynamic_zoom_gl - explicitly enable zooming with active grenade launcher
        scope_texture_alt - alternative sight crosshair
        scope_zoom_factor_alt - alternative sight zoom factor
        scope_dynamic_zoom_alt - enable adjustable scope for alt. sight
        min_scope_zoom_factor - Minimal zoom factor
        snd_shoot_actor_first - custom sound for the first shot
        snd_silncer_shoot_actor_first - custom sound for the first shot with silencer
        base_hud_offset_pos - Editable variables that allow weapon position adjustements that don't require aim tweaks
        base_hud_offset_pos_16x9 - Editable variables that allow weapon position adjustements that don't require aim tweaks
        base_hud_offset_rot - Editable variables that allow weapon position adjustements that don't require aim tweaks
        base_hud_offset_rot_16x9 - Editable variables that allow weapon position adjustements that don't require aim tweaks
        silenced_tracers - Option to disable silencers hiding the tracer on a per weapon basis
        fire_point_silencer - Adjust fire point when silencer is attached, defaults to the value of fire_point. Supports both HUD and world models
		nearwall_zoomed_range - Maximum offset toward camera when aiming down sight close to a wall.
        firepos - Disables g_firepos / g_firepos_zoom for this weapon if set to false.
        aimpos - Disables g_aimpos / g_aimpos_zoom for this weapon if set to false.
        ai_rpm - Set RPM of weapon for AI (only for SSRS)
        motion_mark_reload - Specify motion mark to trigger reload logic, when empty or unspecified uses any motion mark like vanilla code
        modular_attachments - enable modular attachments (https://github.com/themrdemonized/xray-monolith/pull/135)
        modular_scope_group - section which is used to define available scopes (modular attachments)
        inv_scope_x - ui x offset for weapon scope mount (modular attachments)
        inv_scope_y - ui y offset for weapon scope mount (modular attachments)
        attach_base_hud_offset_pos - base aim offset (modular attachments)
        attach_base_hud_offset_rot - base aim rotation (modular attachments)
        attach_mount_hud_offset_pos - scope mount offset (modular_attachments)
        attach_mount_hud_offset_rot - scope mount rotation (modular_attachments)
        attach_scale - scale modifier for all attachments (modular_attachments)
        gl_zoom_factor - Underbarrel grenade launcher aiming zoom factor, default 0.
        hud_fov_aim_factor - Multiplier for the hud_fov_aim_factor console setting while aiming, default 1.0; applied when the console setting is greater than zero.
        cycle_down - Use burst timing at the start of automatic fire, then switch to normal rpm. The initial burst length is derived from fire_modes

    HUD items (the weapon/device section, not its referenced HUD section)
        hud_fov_addition_modifier - Added to the base HUD FOV, default 0.
        nearwall_dist_min, nearwall_dist_max - Near-wall adjustment distances, defaults 0.2 and 1.0.
        nearwall_target_hud_fov - Target HUD FOV near a wall, default 0.27.
        nearwall_speed_mod - Near-wall FOV transition speed, default 10.0.

    Weapon HUD sections (the section referenced by hud)
        shell_particles - Override the weapon's shell particle effect in first person. Omit to inherit the weapon effect; an explicitly empty value disables HUD shell particles.
        fire_bone_silencer - Silenced muzzle bone; falls back to fire_bone, then wpn_body.
        fire_point_silencer - Silenced muzzle offset (x,y,z); falls back to fire_point.

    Inventory item upgrades (weapons, outfits, helmets, backpacks)
        Put these in the upgrade effect section referenced by the upgrade's "section" field:
        inv_grid_x, inv_grid_y - inventory icon position, in grid cells
        inv_grid_width, inv_grid_height - inventory icon size and occupied space, in grid cells
        upgr_icon_x, upgr_icon_y - upgrade picture position, in pixels
        upgr_icon_width, upgr_icon_height - upgrade picture size, in pixels
        inv_name, inv_name_short, description - translated string IDs for this item
        These replace values rather than adding to them. Omitted or empty fields keep their previous values.
        Coordinates must be nonnegative integers; dimensions must be positive integers.
        Only the upgraded item changes. Saved upgrades reapply these values on load.
        If several installed upgrades set the same field, the last applied value wins.
        Existing ui_item text callbacks can override the displayed name and description.
        The icon textures and attachment/layer offsets still come from the base item config.

        fire_point, fire_point2, fire_point_silencer - Replace world-model muzzle offsets. Each requires exactly three comma-separated numbers.
        hud_fire_point, hud_fire_point2, hud_fire_point_silencer - Replace HUD muzzle offsets, also three numbers. These require the item's HUD data to exist when the upgrade is applied.
        rpm_mode_2, cycle_down - Replace burst rate and cycle-down behavior.
        scope_texture, scope_texture_alt - Replace primary/alternative scope UI textures.
        scopes - Additional attachable scope sections, comma-separated. This extension is provided by the bundled aaaa_script_fixes_mp.script patches to item_weapon.

    Grenades
        frags_ap - AP power for shrapnel
        frags_air_resistance - Air resistance for shrapnel
        frags_tracer - Tracer flag for shrapnel
        frags_4to1_tracer - 4 to 1 tracer flag for shrapnel
        frags_magnetic_beam_shot - Magnetic beam flag for shrapnel
        frags_tracer_color_ID - Tracer color ID for shrapnel
        frags_allow_ricochet - Allow shrapnel ricochets, default true. Also applies to other CExplosive objects.
        ammo_grenade_vel - Specify velocity of underbarrel grenade launcher ammo
        explode_effector_sect_name - customizable explode_effector per grenade section
        explode_on_contact - explode on contact
        on_grenade_explode - lua callback

    Explosives
        on_explode - on explode lua callback
	
	PDAs
		nearwall_zoomed_range - Maximum offset toward camera when held up close to a wall.

    Ammo
        tracer_silenced - Silencers can hide bullet tracers on a per ammo type basis
        tracer_length_k - Tracer length modifier

    Detectors
        detector_ui_bone - specifying a custom UI bone for Svarog/Veles in the hud sections of detectors
        lh_lead_gun - Device/Detector animations can now use the lead_gun bone if their hud section has lh_lead_gun = true (script animations can also use this config toggle in their section)

    Flashlight definitions
        hud_mode - toggles hud_mode for lighting, may result in different lighting and shadows

    Anomalies
        blowout_disable_idle - Setting option to true (false by default) in a config will make anomaly temporarily turn off idle particles when anomaly's blowout is triggered, particles are returned upon return to idle state.
        tele_type - New optional telekinesis type for gravitational anomalies behavior
        tele_height_fixed - (default true). If false telekinesis of gravity anomalies will not hard-stop objects at the peak point (tele_height) - they would fluctuate around it instead.
        tele_time
        tele_rotate_speed

    Particles (.pe files)
        update_step - particle update delta in milliseconds

    Hanging lamps and signal lights (object section)
        shadow - Override the main light's shadow flag; omitted uses the spawned lamp's flag.
        volumetric - Override the main light's volumetric flag; omitted uses the spawned lamp's flag.
        ambient_shadow, ambient_volumetric - Shadow/volumetric flags for an existing ambient light, both default false.

    Camera sections
        lim_deg - Interpret lim_yaw and lim_pitch limits in degrees instead of radians, default false.

    PDA level-map sections (game.ltx)
        label - Translated string ID for a label centered on this level's global-map rectangle.
        label_scale_max - When positive, hide the label at or above this global-map zoom and honor pda_show_map_labels. Default 0 leaves this visibility check inactive.
        label_color - R,G,B,A integers from 0 to 255; default 230,220,200,180. If supplied without alpha, alpha is 255.
        label_offset_x, label_offset_y - Offset in global_rect units, both default 0. Positive Y moves the label upward; offsets scale with map zoom.

    Game font sections
        texture2160 - Legacy high-resolution atlas entry, selected from a screen height of 1440 upward when available.
        texture_h<height> - Atlas authored for an explicit screen height, e.g. texture_h1440 or texture_h2160.
        The engine chooses the closest proportional height among explicit entries and the applicable legacy entry (texture800/texture/texture1600/texture2160).
        The matching atlas .ini must exist under textures; unavailable candidates are skipped. Existing string_table/font_prefix suffix rules also apply.

    ImGui font configuration (textures/fonts/<font-name>.ltx beside its .ttf/.otf, section [font])
        sizepixels - Font size in pixels; defaults to the engine's ImGui font size.
        oversampleh, oversamplev - Horizontal/vertical rasterization oversampling, defaults 2 and 1.
        pixelsnaph - Snap horizontal glyph positions to pixels, default false.
        glyphextraspacing - Extra glyph spacing (x,y), default 0,0.
        glyphoffset - Glyph drawing offset (x,y), default 0,0.
        ellipsischar - Ellipsis character code, default 0.
        glyphminadvancex, glyphmaxadvancex - Minimum/maximum horizontal glyph advance, defaults 0 and FLT_MAX.
        rasterizermultiply - Rasterizer brightness multiplier, default 1.0.
        rasterizerdensity - Rasterization density, default 1.0.

    Material overrides (gamedata/materials)
        materials.ltx and material_pairs.ltx contain the complete field reference and examples for adding/overriding gamemtl.xr materials.
        Material-pair sections use material1@material2; breaking_sounds, step_sounds, collide_sounds, collide_particles and collide_marks accept comma-separated resource lists.

	WeaponStatMgun
		snd_shoot: (string) Firing sound.
		snd_empty: (string) Firing sound when out of ammo.
		snd_reload: (string) Sound when reload.
		zoom_factor_def: (float) Zoom scale when holding weapon idle. Zoom closer when the value is higher.
		zoom_factor_aim: (float) Zoom scale when zooming weapon. Zoom closer when the value is higher.
		reload_delay: (float) Reload duration.
		is_single_shot_wpn: (bool) Weapon is single shot.
		unlimited_ammo: (bool) Weapon has unlimited ammo.
		reload_consume: (<script>.<function>(obj)) Return true for the weapon to consume ammo in the gunner's inventory when reload.
		shot_effector: (.anm or empty string for unused) Camera firing effector.
		ammo_class: (string) ammo section useable by this weapon. Can have multiple values seperated by commas.
		ammo_mag_size: (number) Magazine size.
		rpm: Round per minute.
		fire_dispersion_base: (float) Base dispersion of the weapon. Will add up with gunner dispersion. Degree.
		fire_dispersion_owner_scale: (float) How much gunner dispersion affect the final dispersion. Will multiply with gunner dispersion. Lower value mean gunner dispersion contribute less to the final dispersion.
		shell_particles: (.pe) Discarded cartridges particle.
		flame_particles: (.pe) Firing particle.
		smoke_particles: (.pe) Firing particle.
		on_before_use: (<script>.<function>(obj,cam_pos,cam_dir,foot_pos)) Return true to accept actor using the weapon.
		net_spawn_after: (<script>.<function>(obj)) Run right after net_spawn. Allow overriding configurations done in net_spawn.
		on_range_fov: (<script>.<function>(obj,npc,var)) Allow changing gunner visibility range while using machine gun by changing var.range. This function must return "var".
		
		barrels: (string) The weapon can have multiple barrels. This is the barrel sections in userdata file of the weapon visual model. Can have multiple values seperated by commas.
		rpm_range: (min_rpm,max_rpm) Only for weapon with multiple barrels. Each barrel will have a random rpm in this range to create asymmetric firing effect. Use "rpm" if this not exist.
		<barrel_section>@shell_particles: (.pe) Discarded cartridges particle for <barrel_section>. Use "shell_particles" if not exist.
		<barrel_section>@flame_particles: (.pe) Firing particle for <barrel_section>. Use "flame_particles" if not exist.
		<barrel_section>@smoke_particles: (.pe) Firing particle for <barrel_section>. Use "smoke_particles" if not exist.
		
		
		userdata of the weapon visual model:
			[animation_weapon]
			anm_idle, anm_shot, anm_reload0, anm_reload1, anm_chamber: (comma-separated animation names) Weapon-model animation variants.
			magazine_hide_bid: (bone) Optional magazine bone to hide during specified animations.
			magazine_hide_anm: (comma-separated animation names) Animations in which that magazine bone is hidden.

			[mounted_weapon_definition]
			rotate_x_bone: (bone) Bone for vertical rotation.
			rotate_y_bone: (bone) Bone for horizontal rotation.
			rotate_x_speed: (float) Vertical rotation speed. degree/s.
			rotate_y_speed: (float) Horizontal rotation speed. degree/s.
			fire_bone: (bone) Bone where bullets come out.
			drop_bone: (bone) Bone where discarded cartridges particle plays.
			actor_bone: (bone) Bone to attach gunner.
			camera_bone_def: (bone) Bone to attach camera when idle.
			camera_bone_aim: (bone) Bone to attach camera when zoom.
			camera_position: (vector) Relative position to attach camera when using third person camera.
			exit_position: (vector) Relative position to set gunner at when they exits.
			bullet_bones: (bone) Bullet bones to set the visible bullets matching the remaining ammo. Can have multiple values seperated by commas.
			
			[animation]
			idle_body: (string) Gunner idle body animation.
			idle_legs: (string) Gunner idle legs animation.
			
			[animation_hand]
			hand_bid: (bone) Bone to attach hand model.
			hand_pos: (vector) Hand model offset for minor adjustments.
			hand_idle: (string) Hand idle animation.
			
			[camera]
			cam_first: (string) First person camera section. In system.ltx
			cam_chase: (string) Third person camera section. In system.ltx
			
			[sounds]
			volume: (float) Volume.
			rotate_snd: (.ogg) Rotating sound.
			rotate_bid: (bone) Bone where the sound plays.
			rotating_x: (bool) Play sound when rotating vertically.
			rotating_y: (bool) Play sound when rotating horizontally.
			
			[<barrel_section>]
			fire_bone: (bone) Bone where bullets come out.
			drop_bone: (bone) Bone where discarded cartridges particle plays.
	
	Projector
		net_spawn_after: (<script>.<function>(obj)) Run right after net_spawn. Allow overriding configurations done in net_spawn.
		
		userdata of the weapon visual model:
			[projector_definition]
			lights: (string) light sections in this file. Can have multiple values seperated by commas.
			controls: (string) control sections in this file. Can have multiple values seperated by commas.
			
			[<light_section>]
			range: (float) Max range.
			color: (vector 4 float RGBA) Color.
			color_animator: (string) Color animator.
			spot_angle: (float) Spot light angle. degree.
			spot_texture: (string) Spot light texture.
			glow_radius: (float) Glow radius.
			glow_texture: (string) Glow texture.
			light_bone: (bone) Bone to attach the light object.
			guide_bone: (bone) Projector bone. Hide when the light is turned off.
			
			[<control_section>]
			rotate_x_bone: (bone) Bone for vertical rotation.
			rotate_y_bone: (bone) Bone for horizontal rotation.
			rotate_x_speed: (float) Vertical rotation speed. degree/s.
			rotate_y_speed: (float) Horizontal rotation speed. degree/s.
	
	Car
		on_before_hit: (<script>.<function>(obj,hit,bone_id)) Return false to cancel a hit after the engine applies immunity and bone scaling.
		on_before_use: (<script>.<function>(obj,cam_pos,cam_dir,foot_pos)) Return false to reject using the vehicle.
		use_action_hint: (string) Custom interaction hint.

		userdata [car_definition]:
			remote_control: (bool) Allow use without attaching the owner's position to the vehicle, default false.
			camera_bone_def, camera_bone_aim: (bone) Optional idle/aim camera bones.
			zoom_factor_def, zoom_factor_aim: (float) Idle/aim zoom factors, both default 1.0.
			viewport_near: (float) Camera near clipping distance; default -1 uses the normal engine value.
			driving_wheels, steering_wheels, breaking_wheels, exhausts, doors: (bone lists) May be omitted for vehicles without those components. The spelling breaking_wheels is intentional.

		userdata [camera]:
			cam_first, cam_chase, cam_free: (camera section names) Optional overrides for first-person, chase and free cameras.

		/* Drone subclass*/
		control_ele_force: (float) Force to move up/down.
		control_pit_force: (float) Force to move forward/backward.
		control_rol_force: (float) Force to strafe right/left.
		control_yaw_force: (float) Force to turn right/left.
		damping_velocity: (float) Make the drone comes to a stop faster.
		damping_rotation: (float) Reduce wobbling when start/stop moving (x,z). Also yaw rotation comes to a stop faster (y).
		
		userdata
			[drone_definition] Having this section means activating drone subclass.
			drive_bones: (string) bone name list. Apply force to these bone when controlling
			rotor_force: (float) force to rotate each rotor bone. Keep it to just enough to achieve rotor_speed.
			rotor_speed: (float) rotor max rotating speed. Revolutions Per Minute.
			
			[rotors] Rotors of drone subclass
			bone_name = clock:[true/false] /* Rotor bone name = rotating clockwise or counterclockwise  */
		
			[visual_camera_definition]
			enable: (bool) Activate visual camera.
			rotate_x_bone: bone rotating x 
			rotate_y_bone: bone rotating y
			rotate_x_speed: (float) x rotating speed °/s
			rotate_y_speed: (float) y rotating speed °/s
			
			[scopes] /* Having this section means activating scope feature. */
			S0 = bone_camera:1.0
			S1 = bone_camera:2.0
			S2 = bone_camera:6.0
			/* S[level] = [camera bone]:[zoom factor] */
--]]
